language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Hardy's 1729 square: find four different numbers between 1 and 100 such that the sum of the squares of the first two equals the sum of the squares of the other two.
find a, b, c, d : int(1..100)

branching on [a, b, c, d]
such that
$ the four numbers are all different
allDiff([a, b, c, d]),
$ the sum of the squares of a and b equals the sum of the squares of c and d
a * a + b * b = c * c + d * d
